module

public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Simple.Basic
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.McLaughlin.Order
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.McLaughlin.Perfect
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.McLaughlin.Primitive
public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.Subgroup.NormalGeneration

/-!
# Simplicity of the McLaughlin permutation model

The canonical ATLAS model `TauCeti.Sporadic.McL` on `275` points is simple.

Its action on the `275 = 5² * 11` points is faithful, and primitive by the instance of
`McLaughlin.Primitive`; the prime `11` divides the order
`898128000 = 2⁷ * 3⁶ * 5³ * 7 * 11` of the model exactly once (`TauCeti.Sporadic.card_McL`). A
nontrivial normal subgroup of a primitive group acts transitively, so its order is divisible by
`11`, and then its index is not. It therefore contains the element `a * b` of the two ATLAS
generators, whose `11`-th power is `1` by the fourth relator
(`TauCeti.Sporadic.McL.a_mul_b_pow_eleven`). That element normally generates the model, because
the model is perfect (`TauCeti.Sporadic.isPerfect_McL`) and generated by `a` and `b`
(`Subgroup.closure_pair_eq_top_of_eq_closure`): modulo the normal closure of `a * b` the quotient
is generated by the image of `a`, hence cyclic, hence trivial. So the normal subgroup is the whole
model, by `TauCeti.isSimpleGroup_of_normalClosure_eq_top_of_prime_dvd_card`.

The argument is that of `TauCeti.Sporadic.isSimpleGroup_M22`, which applies the same
primitive-action criterion directly, with the generation and power checks and the
perfectness-based normal generation of `TauCeti.Sporadic.isSimpleGroup_HS`.

This proves simplicity of the permutation model, not recognition of the abstract McLaughlin
presentation, whose order is not bounded here.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.isSimpleGroup_McL`: the ATLAS permutation model of `McL` is simple.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `McLG1-p275B0`, <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/>.
* J. McLaughlin, *A simple group of order 898,128,000*, in *Theory of Finite Groups*
  (Harvard Symposium), Benjamin, New York, 1969, 109–111.
* J. D. Dixon and B. Mortimer, *Permutation Groups*, §1.6, for normal subgroups of primitive
  groups.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.Sporadic

/-- The canonical 275-point permutation model of the McLaughlin group is simple. -/
instance isSimpleGroup_McL : IsSimpleGroup McL := by
  have hgen := Subgroup.closure_pair_eq_top_of_eq_closure McL.a_mem McL.b_mem McL_def
  have hpow : (⟨McL.a, McL.a_mem⟩ * ⟨McL.b, McL.b_mem⟩ : McL) ^ 11 = 1 :=
    Subtype.ext McL.a_mul_b_pow_eleven
  exact isSimpleGroup_of_normalClosure_eq_top_of_prime_dvd_card (X := Fin 275)
    Nat.prime_eleven (by simp) (by rw [card_McL]; norm_num) _ hpow
    (Subgroup.normalClosure_singleton_mul_eq_top _ _ hgen)

end TauCeti.Sporadic
